  "all_ingredients_flat": "Brown rice, Grated coconut, Black eyed peas, Mustard seeds, Asafetida, Green chilli, Curry leaves, Salt, Water",
  "instructions": "BROWN RICE FLOUR: Soak 1/2 cup of brown rice in water for 30 minutes, drain the water and spread the rice in a towel to dry for 10 minutes, grind the dried rice in a mixie to a smooth powder. Use a sieve to get fine powder. Grind the residue and sieve again. This process can be repeated twice or more. Dry roast the fine powder till it's warm (may be 2 or 3 minutes) and let it cool to room temperature. This will yield about 3/4 cups of rice flour.\n\nBLACK EYED PEAS: Soak in water for some time, cook & drain.\n\n(1) Heat a dry pan, add half a teaspoon of mustard seeds and let it splutter.\n(2) Add asafetida, chopped green chillies, and curry leaves.\n(3) Add 1.5 cups of water and salt to taste and bring it to boil.\n(4) Reduce the heat and mix in 3/4 cup of brown rice flour. After the dough is formed add 1 tablespoon of cooked and drained black eyed peas.\n(5) Let the dough cool a bit and then make into lemon sized balls.\n(6) Flatten each ball in idli plate and make a small hole in the middle.\n(7) Steam for about 5 minutes.",
